# This file constrains the versions pip is allowed to resolve, including inside the PEP 517
# build-isolation environments it creates for every source distribution it builds.
# NOTE: This is a CMake template file. The actual constraints.txt is generated during CMake
#       configuration and exported to pip as PIP_CONSTRAINT and PIP_BUILD_CONSTRAINT (see below).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: when pip builds a package from source it creates a fresh, isolated
#       environment for that package's build requirements. The --no-binary / --only-binary format
#       control from python3.cmake does propagate into that environment, but the version pins from
#       requirements.txt do NOT. PyOpenGL_accelerate declares an unbounded "numpy" build
#       requirement, so without this file it compiles against whatever numpy is newest on PyPI
#       instead of the numpy we ship, and drags in a source build of that numpy along the way.
#
# KEEP THIS FILE MINIMAL. A constraint applies to every environment pip resolves, nested build
#       environments included. Constraining setuptools, wheel or meson-python here would make the
#       build unsatisfiable on CY2023-CY2025, whose numpy versions hard-pin their own
#       setuptools==59.2.0 / wheel==0.37.0 / meson-python<0.16.0 build requirements.
#
# Constraint files may not contain direct references (name @ url), extras or markers, unlike
#       requirements files. Bare "name==version" entries only.
#
# To update these versions, edit RV_DEPS_NUMPY_VERSION / RV_DEPS_CYTHON_VERSION in
#       cmake/defaults/CY*.cmake
#
# This file is exported to pip as BOTH PIP_CONSTRAINT and PIP_BUILD_CONSTRAINT. On pip < 26.2, PIP_CONSTRAINT alone reaches build-isolation environments; pip
#       >= 26.2 deprecated that and requires PIP_BUILD_CONSTRAINT to constrain them instead. Since RV_PYTHON_BUILD_DEPS installs an unpinned "pip", the
#       version actually in play at build time can be either, so both variables must be set.

numpy==@_numpy_version@
@_cython_constraint@
